            "review_title": "Review at Ryoshi Sushi Ikeikemaru",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nOne of the worst Japanese foods I've tasted\nNov 2016 • Family\nConveyor belt sushi is a fun and efficient concept for sushi value chains developed in Japan. Had fond memories of those in Japan and Singapore... but this one is NOTHING like those.\n\nIt's bad in so many ways:\n- seating was slow and ineffective even in a non-peak hour\n- the sushi rice here is dry and crumbly that it falls apart easily\n- the ingredients on the top of the sushi looks messy and not fresh\n- the plates of sushi available are always the same few dishes - those that are easiest to make - the chef there is either lazy or incompetent to make more varieties to entice customers - which is the whole point of conveyor belt sushi restaurants in the first place!\n- the food just don't taste good\n\nWe walked out. Never to return.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 31, 2017",
