            "review_text": "Simeon T\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam182 contributions\n0\nDreadful Experience\nJul 2017 • Friends\nLocated on B2 of the Takashimaya Shopping Centre, you would think that the experience would be one to remember. It was, one to remember not to come back.\n\nThe service was dreadful, waiting at the front of the restaurant to be seated should have been the first sign to walk away, we were ignored and they weren't that busy. Once seated, drinks took for ever. As it is a conveyor belt style restaurant, another indicator that we should have looked else where, plates weren't cleared in a timely fashion, if at all. The service simply was horrible. You could tell the staff didn't want to be there.\n\nThe food offerings were mediocre at best as they came around on the conveyor but, the prices reflected that of a calibre they weren't even serving on their a la carte option. I've enjoyed similar style restaurants in the past but, this one wasn't anything that anyone should endure, let alone pay for.\nRead more\nWritten August 13, 2017",
